# Document previews

Documents in the CRM must remain previewable — not download-only — but **chat attachments must not auto-load or auto-download** (that disrupts scrolling and UX).

## Required behavior

- Mail/chat attachments: show a compact file row (name, size, type) with **Preview** / **Download**. Load PDF/image/text/media **only after** the user clicks Preview. Never auto-embed `object`/`iframe` for office or unknown types (browsers often force a download).
- Quotes/invoices: keep the existing preview modal/document view wired and opening correctly; PDF attachments saved to chat history must use `application/pdf` so the on-demand canvas preview can run.
- Newsletter/email editors: the live preview iframe (or equivalent) must reflect the document the user is editing.

## Do not

- Auto-fetch or auto-render attachment bytes when a chat bubble mounts.
- Leave documents as download-only when a preview path already exists (`MessageAttachments` Preview toggle, `QuoteDocument`, `InvoiceDocument`, mailing preview iframe).
- Save quote/invoice PDFs without persisting them as reply attachments with a PDF mime type.
